> git tag -a <tag-name>


Annotated Tags

> Use "git tag -a" to create a new annotated tag. Git will then open your default
  text editor and prompt you for additional information.

> Similar to git commit, we can also use the -m option to pass a message directly
  and forgo the opening of the text editor

> git status
> git clone url
> touch test.txt
> git status
> git commit -am "New change"
> git tag -a v26.1.0

